we're approaching the end of the year  and for many that means work is winding  down and we get to go home and hang out  with family and friends for the holidays  it also gives us time to play a bunch of  video games here's what's coming to  Playstation Plus this month and some  recommendations for games to play with  your family and friends over the  holidays  [Music]  before we jump into what's coming to the  game and Classics catalog this month a  quick reminder that you can still grab  December's monthly games they're  available until January 2nd if you're a  PlayStation Plus essential extra or  premium Member First up is Mass Effect  legendary edition for PlayStation 4. the  remaster of the iconic Mass Effect  Trilogy as Commander Shepard assemble  your team and defend the Galaxy against  Reapers which are conspiring to bring  about the extinction of all organic life  legendary edition features Mass Effect 1  2 and 3 and over 40 pieces of DLC from  armor and weapons packs to MIDI single  player stories like layer of the Shadow  broker and the Beloved Citadel DLC next  up is divine knockout Founders Edition  for PlayStation 4 and PlayStation 5  which launched straight onto PlayStation  Plus earlier this month play as one of  10 playable gods including mimir and  Thor as you battle to boot enemies out  of the Arena Founders Edition includes  bonus content for the game as well as a  character skin in Smite your final  monthly game for December is bio mutant  for PlayStation 4 and Playstation 5. a  post-apocalyptic game where you can mix  all manner of combat styles from martial  arts to guns and add in some mutant  abilities to boot if you're a  PlayStation Plus extra or premium member  you have access to the game catalog and  there are a number of great games  joining this model it's time to step  back into the ring with WWE 2k22 with  new controls the in-ring action has  never felt better and in the 2K showcase  mode you can relive iconic moments from  Rey Mysterio's career build your  All-Star roster in my faction and become  a WWE general manager in my GM WWE 2k22  will be available from January 3rd to  March 13th and when you're done  wrestling hope county is waiting for you  in Far Cry 5 as a sheriff's deputy it's  up to you to take on Joseph's seed  leader of the Doomsday called Eden's  gate and rid Montana of his influence  team up with a friend in Co-op or  recruit and in-game pal like  cheeseburger the bear if you want to  spend more time in Hope County then  you're in luck Far Cry New Dawn is also  joining game catalog this Standalone  spin-off is set in Hope County's 17  years after a nuclear event wrecked the  whole place it's not exactly the murky  post-apocalypse you might expect as the  nuclear fallout has created a luscious  Super Bloom creating a wacky and  colorful environment to explore but if  you fancy going back to the basics  somewhat then give Far Cry Primal a shot  Primal takes you back to the Stone Age  where the beasts that walk the earth can  give you just as much trouble as a rival  tribe craft Spears clubs and arrows and  tame creatures like saber-toothed tigers  to help you face off any threats as you  explore looking for a fantasy world to  get lost in then take on the Dual role  of Gondor Ranger Italian and elf wraith  Keller brimbor in Middle Earth Shadow of  Mordor and its sequel shadow of War  explore the wastes of Mordor and get  revenge for the death of your family by  tearing through the ranks of Orcs using  the game's Dynamic Nemesis system but if  you're sick of being a good guy try out  Evil Genius 2 become a criminal  mastermind and build out your lair with  enough nefarious traps and minions to  keep the forces of Justice at Bay Evil  Genius 2 is full of heavy knots to  Classic spy films and it's funny to boot  now it's time for me to get on my Yakuza  soapbox three more games are joining the  game catalog meaning there's really no  excuse not to give the Fantastic  franchise a go Yakuza 6 the song of life  is the final game with series  protagonist Kazama Kiryu at the helm so  you can now experience his entire Saga  and one spot Yakuza like a dragon  switches things up drastically and is a  great game to play if you want to dip  your toe into Yakuza without committing  to the whole series you play as Ichiban  a Yakuza grunt sent to prison for a  murder he didn't commit after he's freed  and sent back into a world and a yak is  a family that has moved on without him  Yakuza games are usually Brawlers but  like a dragon switches things on its  head and it's turn base the melodrama  and heart at the core of Yakuza games is  still there so like a dragon is a  perfect jumping off point judgment a yak  is a spin-off also joins the catalog  instead of playing as a member of the  Yakuza you play as detective takayuki  yugami who's working to get to the  bottom of a series of murders in Tokyo I  am hopping off my Yakuza soapbox now  thank me later next up is Mortal shell  as the foundling you take on the rotten  world of fall Grim in sort of a spirit  form enemies can easily kill you in this  form so it's up to you to find find a  mortal shell so you can square off  against them the shells allow for a lot  of variety and gameplay and if you're a  fan of from soft Souls games this is  worth a try for more family-friendly  offerings take an underwater adventure  with Finn Jake and all your Adventure  Time Pals and Adventure Time pirates of  the encouridion or stop fiendish aliens  in Ben 10 power trip if a dinosaur  adventure is more your thing  gigantosaurus the game is the one for  you looking to exercise your brain  muscles The Pedestrian is a quirky take  on a puzzle platformer where you move  road signs around to create a path  through the environment but if you fancy  a deep RPG to sink some hours into check  out pillars of Eternity 2 deadfire  Ultimate Edition chase a rogue God  across the unexplored land and chart  your own adventure in an RPG built on  DND gameplay also joining the game  catalog this month are worms wmd and the  escapists 2 from 1817 worms wmd Remains  the experience of classic worms games  but has a Fresh coat of paint and some  new mechanics to really up the Mayhem  carefully plot and execute your escape  from prison in The Escapist 2 where how  you escape is up to you if you're a  PlayStation Plus premium member you also  have access to the classics game catalog  full of games from previous PlayStation  Generations this month it's time to put  the pedal to the metal as Ridge Racer 2  joins the catalog or you can hit the  tables in pinball Heroes and speaking of  Heroes when a haunting Vision disturbs  Abe's retirement it's up to him to  discover the secret of the Soul storm  brew and save the trap muticons in odd  World Abe's Exodus if you missed ninja  Theory's cult classic Heavenly sword  which stars Andy Circus it's also  available to stream in the classics  catalog  if you've got some down time to spend  with friends and family this winter then  what better way to bond than to play  some video games together here's my pick  of games from the game catalog that are  perfect to play together overcook 2 has  the potential to make your friendship  stronger or ruin them all together you  work as chefs preparing a series of  meals but one person can't do everything  themselves so you gotta work together to  get those orders out it's a lot of  chaotic fun with simple controls that  everyone can handle in a similar vein  moving out is full of Mayhem in Fun For  All of the family as a Furniture  Arrangement and relocation technician  it's up to you and your pals to help  move furniture from one place to another  but no one said you had to be careful  about it nidhog is simple to learn and  difficult to master with minimal inputs  and frantic one-on-one action this  fencing game will have everyone playing  and watching yelling at the screen in no  time the sequel is also on game catalog  too it might be a little cold to hit the  links in this weather but that doesn't  mean that golf is off the table  completely with everybody's golf you and  three others can face off on a number of  colorful and quirky courses if you fancy  something a little more story driven  definitely give Brothers A Tale of Two  Sons ago you can either play alone or  with one other person controlling the  brothers as they search for a cure for  their father's illness the game tells a  beautiful story set against a colorful  backdrop inspired by Nordic myths be  warned though it can get a little  emotional but at least you can Bond over  it with whoever you're playing with what  are you going to be playing on  PlayStation Plus this month let us know  and make sure to shout out your hidden  gems below you can find me on Twitter at  Devonte Chisholm and I'll see you next  month for your January games  [Music]  foreign  [Music]

